 thunderstorms. Heavy rain falling on saturated soils and\nburn scars could lead to localized flash flooding and rises on\nlocal rivers.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-30T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Uncompahgre Plateau/Dallas Divide; Northwestern San Juan Mountains; Southwest San Juan Mountains; Paradox Valley/Lower Dolores River; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bd99f2cf2c456b0afdad64dc05567baddbab62ce.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bd99f2cf2c456b0afdad64dc05567baddbab62ce.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-29T05:44:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 290544 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1144 PM MDT Mon Sep 28 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered to widespread precipitation showers and storms continue. - Increased flooding concerns for rain-soaked terrain, especially within and adjacent to the southern San Juans. - A Flood Watch is in effect for southeast Utah and southwest Colorado thro","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-28T19:09:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Deep moisture will continue to stream in from the southwest bringing widespread rain and a few embedded thunderstorms over the next few days. A Flood Watch has been issued for southeast UT and southwest CO due to the increased rainfall and flooding risks. All the clouds and precipitation will keep fire weather concerns to a minimum. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHO","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"hot02","station_name":"CSU Rogers Mesa Research Sta","distance_km":5.9,"soil_temp_5cm_f":61.18,"soil_temp_15cm_f":63.